{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1095290-mandragora-garden-and-cruac-rituals","id":1095290,"title":"Mandragora Garden and Cruac rituals.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-21T16:51:58-07:00","id":1095290,"title":"Mandragora Garden and Cruac rituals.","content":"I was looking for cruac rituals that will work with Mandragora Garden, and I couldn't really find any that lasts for a scene. Does anyone know of any that I was missing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T17:47:41-07:00","id":1095305,"title":"","content":"Check out Blood Sorcery - Sacraments and Blasphemies. You can make something last a scene by adding a few target successes. It really fleshes out the Blood Sorcery system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T20:01:10-07:00","id":1095337,"title":"","content":"As far as I know, it works the same for rituals that last for more than a scene too, so Blood Price should work fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T21:42:41-07:00","id":1096163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1095290-mandragora-garden-and-cruac-rituals?p=1095337#post1095337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I know, it works the same for rituals that last for more than a scene too, so Blood Price should work fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it? It never said that in the book, but it does sound like a good idea. I just didn't understand why they used the word scene instead of night because most of the rituals I found lasted a night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T21:44:22-07:00","id":1096164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1095290-mandragora-garden-and-cruac-rituals?p=1095305#post1095305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Check out Blood Sorcery - Sacraments and Blasphemies. You can make something last a scene by adding a few target successes. It really fleshes out the Blood Sorcery system.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was never particularly a fan of the blood sorcery book because it kind of forced specialization in one theme of blood sorcery, and part of blood sorcery's power was its varied abilities in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T12:52:44-07:00","id":1096451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1095290-mandragora-garden-and-cruac-rituals?p=1096163#post1096163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it? It never said that in the book, but it does sound like a good idea. I just didn't understand why they used the word scene instead of night because most of the rituals I found lasted a night.</div> </div> </div> </div>IRRC, someone involved with the book said they meant a scene or longer and it slipped through the cracks of editing. It makes no sense to say scene long rituals can be indefinite but not night long rituals, at least to me. There may be a reason for certain rituals to be ineligible, but not simply because the effect already lasts more than a scene. An argument might can be made for something lasting longer than a night already, but I don't remember a ritual that works that way off the top of my head. I imagine if such an example exists there will be another reason to exclude it than it isn't a scene long effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T20:24:37-07:00","id":1096580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1095290-mandragora-garden-and-cruac-rituals?p=1096451#post1096451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IRRC, someone involved with the book said they meant a scene or longer and it slipped through the cracks of editing. It makes no sense to say scene long rituals can be indefinite but not night long rituals, at least to me. There may be a reason for certain rituals to be ineligible, but not simply because the effect already lasts more than a scene. An argument might can be made for something lasting longer than a night already, but I don't remember a ritual that works that way off the top of my head. I imagine if such an example exists there will be another reason to exclude it than it isn't a scene long effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, that makes sense. So just to be sure, the rituals cast on the garden effect the garden and not the vampire in the garden, right? If that's the case, what rituals would be good for being cast indefinitely on the garden.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T10:49:45-07:00","id":1096794,"title":"","content":"I don't remember anybody saying that part of the text wasn't spot on. It says the indefinite rituals are cast on the garden so I stick with that. Hopefully, Half-Damned clears up how mandragora work in R2. Being able to use a mandragora as hands and eyes does not necessarily mean a keeper can feel and see what the mandragora does, so Cheval might be unnecessary or almost a requirement. Blood Price seems good as long as mandragora can &quot;drink&quot; blood normally. With a human ghoul to feed the garden, a keeper will not be easy to imprison. Gorgon's Gaze or Touch of the Morrigan for defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T19:00:25-07:00","id":1097933,"title":"","content":"Having Gorgon Gaze on full time would be too much of a nightmare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T05:20:18-07:00","id":1098072,"title":"","content":"Since mandragora count as eyes for rituals, I would say the Acolyte could choose for the plant to go &quot;blind&quot; as long as the plant was also the one petrifying. Other interpretations are possible and some would be problematic, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}